"""Task 243: a column added by SUMMARIZE / SUMMARIZECOLUMNS / ROW / GENERATE that holds a Variant, read by an iterator under a type test, and the table builders under a Variant.

Every expected answer is a live Power BI answer on the Facts table of tools.dax_oracle_diff (6 rows: Sales, Quantity, Region, Note), or on a second Facts table
(SECOND_ROWS, where the data-dependent conditions flip) or a third (THIRD_ROWS, where some regions hold only blank notes).

The measured rule, in plain words:
  * A column that SUMMARIZE, SUMMARIZECOLUMNS, ROW or GENERATE adds is typed like one that ADDCOLUMNS or SELECTCOLUMNS adds: when its expression is an IF, SWITCH,
    COALESCE or IFERROR whose branches differ in class (a text beside a number, a True/False beside a number, a Currency beside a text ...) it is a Variant,
    whatever the groups hold.  MAXX, MINX, SUMX, AVERAGEX and COUNTX over a Variant column read only the numbers in it: a column whose groups all hold a text
    gives BLANK, and ISSTRING of it is False (REVIEW_ROWS: ISSTRING(MAXX(SUMMARIZE(Facts,Facts[Region],"s",COALESCE(MAX(Facts[Note]),0)),[s])) is False, the
    engine said True).  A Variant is a Variant even when the condition is a constant (IF(TRUE(),"abc",7)).
  * A number that is beside a date makes a plain number column (the dates are numbers).
  * A text that fails to convert inside an iterator over a table built by ADDCOLUMNS / SELECTCOLUMNS / SUMMARIZE / GROUPBY raises under every type test, where the same
    text read from the loaded column is answered by the type for the tests that do not depend on the value.
  * Stays refused (unsure => refused, Power BI answers or raises, the engine does not model it): TOPN ordered by a column that holds a True/False beside a number;
    the groups of a SUMMARIZECOLUMNS whose Variant column takes a text beside a number and reads data in two of its branches, the groups of a SUMMARIZE whose added column
    reads HASONEVALUE / SELECTEDVALUE / VALUES or takes a date beside a text, the groups of a GROUPBY whose aggregate reads a text column (their order differs from
    the order of the first rows); a SUMMARIZE over FILTER / TOPN / CALCULATETABLE whose added column reads data (Power BI sees only the rows of that table, the engine counts
    every row of the group); a number-type test of an iterator whose body returns a Variant column in a branch (typed by the value taken); AVERAGEX of a Variant column with a
    Currency branch under a type test (a Currency in Power BI).
  * ROW, DATATABLE and SAMPLE join the names that change the context (a Variant below them stays refused); the other names of the list were there already.
ANSWERED holds 330 probes on the first table, ANSWERED_SECOND 330 on the second, ANSWERED_THIRD 330 on the third, STILL_REFUSED the shapes Power BI answers (or raises for) and the engine refuses.
"""

